Call pairs: every recipe child gets its own request and reply pair at spawn, dup'd onto the
descriptors AMK_CALL and AMK_REPLY already name, served while make waits for children or for
a jobserver token, and dropped with the child, so concurrent callers never read each other's
replies and a request left unread dies with its recipe. A forked guest's and a deferred
call's variable writes ride a pipe that one collector reads beside the child's output,
applying whole records as they arrive, and a printed goal's value comes up the job's mail.
The tagged reply FIFOs, their directory under TMPDIR, the temp file queues, and amk_mkfifo
are gone: nothing amk makes under TMPDIR but the serve socket.

